WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.256
Raise your hand, and be honest, if&nbsp;
you've used the phrase "crazy busy"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.717 --> 00:00:08.465
to describe your day,

00:00:09.089 --> 00:00:10.563
your week,

00:00:10.563 --> 00:00:12.225
your&nbsp;month.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.653
I'm an emergency-room doctor,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.175
and "crazy busy" is a phrase 
you will never hear&nbsp;me use.

00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:26.644
Step one to go from Crazy Mode to 
Ready Mode is to relentlessly triage.

00:00:26.644 --> 00:00:29.089
In Crazy&nbsp;Mode, you're always 
busy, always stressed,

00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:32.815
because you're reacting to every 
challenge with&nbsp;the same response.

00:00:33.439 --> 00:00:37.452
Contrast that with Ready 
Mode, where we triage,

00:00:37.452 --> 00:00:41.095
which means we prioritize&nbsp;
by degree of urgency.

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:44.114
Red -- immediately life-threatening.

00:00:44.114 --> 00:00:47.790
Yellow -- serious, but not&nbsp;
immediately life-threatening.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:49.530
Green -- minor.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.384
And we focus our efforts
 first on the reds.

00:00:53.384 --> 00:00:57.470
So&nbsp;start by triaging correctly.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.476
Know your reds.

